javascript.q:
Coding Challenge: (JavaScript) LRU cache. Design an LRU cache with a fixed capacity supporting get(key) and put(key, value) in O(1) average time. get returns -1 for a missing key and put evicts the least recently used entry when capacity is exceeded. Example: capacity 2; put(1,1); put(2,2); get(1) -> 1; put(3,3) evicts key 2; get(2) -> -1. Constraints: capacity >= 1; up to 100000 operations. Starter signature in JavaScript:
class LRUCache {
  constructor(capacity) {}
  get(key) {}
  put(key, value) {}
}

